# gh — real-world examples

## Authentication

```sh
gh auth login        # interactive; choose SSH so pushes use your key
gh auth status
gh auth setup-git    # use gh as git's credential helper
gh auth switch
gh auth token
gh auth logout
```

## Core command groups

```text
gh auth | browse | codespace | gist | issue | org
gh pr | project | release | repo
```

## View the current repo's README

```sh
gh repo view
```

## Issues: list, view one, create one

```sh
gh issue list
gh issue view 1
gh issue create      # interactive prompts
```

## Create a pull request from a feature branch

```sh
gh pr create         # interactive prompts
```

## Check out someone's PR locally for review

```sh
gh pr checkout 42
```

## Create a public gist and open it in the browser

```sh
gh gist create hello.py -d "my Hello-World program in Python" -w -p
```

## Create a custom label for issues and PRs

```sh
gh label create do-not-merge
```

## Homelab workflow: clone, new private repo, cut a release

```sh
gh repo clone ireaneus/ireaneus-cheatsheets
gh repo create homelab-scripts --private --source . --push
gh release create v1.0 --notes "first stable homelab release"
```
